0,Nkoroo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nkoroo_language,"Language family. Niger–Congo?Nkoroo. Nkọrọọ is an Ijaw language spoken by about 4,500 ethnic Nkọrọ in Rivers State, Nigeria. Nkọrọ has significantly influenced the Defaka language.[2].",Nkoroo,Niger-Congo
1,Nkoroo Language (NKX) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/nkx/,"Nkoroo is a stable indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.",Nkoroo,Niger-Congo
